cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use photonics-helper in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "photonics-helper: photonics, fiber-optics and nonlinear-optics helpers for Python"
abstract: >-
  A Python library providing a stable foundation for photonics computation:
  type-safe units and constants, temporal/spectral grids, an auditable optical
  material database, and a suite of nonlinear-optics tools (GNLSE propagation,
  soliton and breather analysis, Raman response and noise, phase-matching
  diagnostics, chi-squared mixing, DBR/TMM stacks, FROG retrieval, structured
  light), validated against results from the literature.
